' --- manual: everything below this line is hand-authored; the script preserves it ---

' The automated pass reads data members and nothing else, so all three classes
' arrive as empty boxes: two are static-method surfaces and the third holds one
' string. The blocks below fill those boxes, give them the colours the
' conventions table asks for, and draw the composition the transfer helper
' performs.
'
' They use fully-qualified class names rather than a reopened namespace block,
' because this PlantUML version crashes when a namespace that already holds
' classes is declared a second time. Redeclaring a class merges its members
' into the box the automated pass already drew, so a refresh keeps both.

class ores::storage::net::http_client #ECECEC {
    {static} +get(url : string, dest : path) : void
    {static} +put(url : string, src : path) : void
    {static} +put_returning_body(url : string, src : path) : string
}
note right of "ores::storage::net::http_client"
The only part that knows about sockets: Boost.Beast and
Boost.Asio over plain TCP, http:// only. Both directions
stream through a file_body, so a multi-megabyte package
never sits in memory. get reads the status line before it
touches the destination file.
end note

class ores::storage::filesystem::archiver #ECECEC {
    {static} +pack(src_dir : path, dest_archive : path) : void
    {static} +extract(archive : path, dest_dir : path) : void
}
note right of "ores::storage::filesystem::archiver"
libarchive, a .tar.gz in and out. The component's one
platform difference sits here: on Windows the wide libarchive
entry points are used, because a std::filesystem::path
yields wchar_t there.
end note

class ores::storage::net::storage_transfer #ECECEC {
    +storage_transfer(http_base_url : string)
    +pack(src_dir : path, dest_archive : path) : void
    +unpack(archive : path, dest_dir : path) : void
    +upload(bucket : string, key : string, src_file : path) : void
    +upload_returning_response(bucket : string, key : string, src_file : path) : string
    +download(bucket : string, key : string, dest_file : path) : void
    +pack_and_upload(src_dir : path, bucket : string, key : string) : void
    +fetch_and_unpack(bucket : string, key : string, dest_dir : path) : void
    +upload_blob(bucket : string, key : string, data : span<const char>) : void
    +download_blob(bucket : string, key : string) : vector<char>
}
note right of "ores::storage::net::storage_transfer"
The surface the callers use. The first four methods are
the atomic operations; the rest compose them, staging
through ores.platform's scoped temp file, and the two blob
methods gzip through ores.utility on the way past. Every
method logs at debug with bucket, key, bytes and duration.
end note

